    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0387" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00113 E.W./9–1644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-30T19:00:00-04:00">October 30, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9052. Department’s 6485 of August 16. In view of absence of any official British
                    or Russian response to our proposal and questions posed in 4037 from
                        Moscow<anchor n="33" xml:id="d185-f1"/> (repeated to London from Moscow as
                    232, October 22) please defer further action along lines of Department’s 8689 of
                    October 19 until decisions have been reached here on these questions.</p>
                <p>Similar instructions have been sent to Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
